(
    title: "3-D Havoc",
    developer: Some("VideoSoft"),
    description: Some("You pilot a stellar cruiser trapped in an asteroid field, steering with the joystick and firing at the rocks; the left difficulty switch raises and lowers your shield, which drops a little with every asteroid that hits you. After around a dozen kills the view changes to a first-person tunnel where enemy craft attack. The display uses an anaglyph 3-D effect that the Color/B&W switch turns on and off, so it can be played without red/blue glasses. The prototype stops short of an ending: past the \"HERO\" screen shots stop connecting, the fuel gauge is dead, and the game never finishes."),
